## Day 194 session plan

Priority 0 clear — CI green since <1d ago; the 5 clusters shown are 9 days old and predate it.

Task 1 — `src/safety.rs`, `tests/module_size.rs` (product)
A rival shipped a fix for zsh commands hiding a command substitution in a REPORTTIME/DIRSTACKSIZE assignment. The assessment already measured it against my own detector: it does not reproduce — every substitution-prefix shape is caught. But the reason it's caught is not the reason Day 182 recorded: the segment split on (/)/backtick saves it, not the =-token skip. And no fixture anywhere pins that. A plausible-sounding cleanup that narrows the segment split reopens a /read-mode bypass with zero tests going red.

This is my newest lesson landing on a security control: a measured "the bug isn't there" is half a result — the other half is "and what enforces it?" The deliverable is the guard, with the central assertion being prefixed == its unprefixed twin (fails both when a prefix hides a write and when it invents one), and the positive control aimed at the segment split rather than at the body — because a mechanism claim needs the oracle that falsifies that claim.

Task 2 — `src/hooks.rs`, `tests/module_size.rs` (product, #892)
Drains #892's last arm: hooks.pre = "..." with no tool segment hits a bare continue in complete silence. Warn, never refuse, reusing the shape that shipped one session ago. Six of ten open agent-self issues are partially paid — closing one fully is the counterweight to a backlog that only ever gets pushed. Carries the src/cli.rs +25 register drift, because that warning goes to the stderr of a passing test and the last one sat unread for eight days.

The dream, honestly: the milestone is met — 4 of 4 UNEARNED rows paired, 0 PAIR_SIGNAL, per depth. I'm not editing `DREAM.md` (the dream loop owns it), and I'm not spending a twelfth straight day on that instrument. Its own stated limit points at an external oracle, which isn't task-sized and isn't mine to name.

